You have a general-purpose v2 storage account named contosomedia that stores final video packages under the releases/ path, plus a set of renditions flagged with a blob index tag. You edited the account's lifecycle policy in Code View, and the saved policy applies a rule that matches candidate blobs by path prefix and by blob index tag before moving them to the cool tier after 45 days without modification.

```json
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "name": "RetirePackages",
      "enabled": true,
      "type": "Lifecycle",
      "definition": {
        "filters": {
          "blobTypes": ["BlockBlob"],
          "prefixes": ["releases/"],
          "tagMatches": [
            { "name": "expire", "op": "eq", "value": "true" }
          ]
        },
        "actions": {
          "baseBlob": {
            "tierToCool": { "daysAfterModificationGreaterThan": 45 }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Your team wants the policy to manage every blob under the releases/ path, and also every blob carrying the expire=true tag, including blobs that match just the path prefix or just the tag. Which change to the policy should you make?

You have a premium block blob storage account named contosabuild that holds finished CI build artifacts. The team wants the account's lifecycle policy to reduce the storage consumed by artifacts that have aged out, and they have observed that the policy runs to completion without changing where the artifacts are stored or how much capacity they use.

The policy, maintained in Code View, currently reads:

```json
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "name": "AgeArtifacts",
      "enabled": true,
      "type": "Lifecycle",
      "definition": {
        "filters": {
          "blobTypes": ["BlockBlob"]
        },
        "actions": {
          "baseBlob": {
            "tierToCool": { "daysAfterModificationGreaterThan": 30 }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Which change should you make?

You have a general-purpose v2 storage account named contosorecords that stores regulated record datasets as block blobs. Blob versioning is enabled on the account, and the export job takes a snapshot of a dataset each time that dataset is refreshed. The account's lifecycle policy is maintained in Code View and currently reads:

```json
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "name": "CoolCurrentBlobs",
      "enabled": true,
      "type": "Lifecycle",
      "definition": {
        "filters": {
          "blobTypes": ["BlockBlob"]
        },
        "actions": {
          "baseBlob": {
            "tierToCool": { "daysAfterModificationGreaterThan": 60 },
            "delete": { "daysAfterModificationGreaterThan": 365 }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Only one rule is present, and its action block applies to the current version of each blob rather than to previous versions or snapshots. The records team wants old previous versions and old snapshots removed once they are 30 days old, while the current version of every blob must keep the treatment it has today. Which change to the policy should you make?

